From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Phononenom <64574232+Phononenom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:44:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the host heap gives memory back,
 and the GPU threads wait for it

headless/heap_arenas.inc, heap_pages.cpp, performance.cpp: the heap balloon (inflated while a write waits,
deflated after 10 s of calm; EDEN_HEAP_BALLOON=0 turns it off), a quiet page-in and a recovery without the
driver step (both avoided a deadlock in the arena lock), the GPU threads waiting for memory in the new
handler (EDEN_NEW_WAIT_GPU_MS) and recovering it every 100 ms, the loaded shader programs dropped at the
first memory wait (EDEN_SHADER_PROGRAMS_KEEP=1 keeps them), the pool's free bytes for the read-through
window, fiber stacks sized from use.

From these commits (oldest first):
- 2026-11-19 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the heap trim asks the NUP caches first, and the report says what they hold
- 2026-11-20 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: where the heap's idle memory sits (a measure)
- 2026-11-20 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: smaller fiber stacks and the flexible pool measured (step S1)
- 2026-11-20 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: S1's flexible-memory import is a plain one
- 2026-11-20 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the heap trimmed while a write waits; the pool's free pieces measured
- 2026-11-21 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the heap's free runs given back while a game write waits
- 2026-11-21 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the heap give-back takes pages back without the recovery
- 2026-11-22 Playtendoh's Switch 2 side: the heap give-back's page-in packs cold game memory again
